{
    "background_story": "Gian was a young anthropologist fascinated by the indigenous cultures of the Pacific Northwest. His research led him to the Chinookan people, a tribe that once thrived along the Columbia River. As he delved deeper into their traditions and customs, Gian became particularly drawn to their rich storytelling heritage. He spent years learning the Chinookan language and transcribing ancient tales passed down through generations. Gian's dedication earned him the respect of the Chinookan community, who welcomed him as one of their own. He went on to help preserve their cultural legacy, working closely with tribal elders to create a comprehensive archive of Chinookan stories, songs, and histories. Gian's work not only helped to revitalize the Chinookan language but also fostered a new era of cross-cultural understanding and appreciation.",
